@* The shell is the composition root: it is the one place allowed to see every
   context at once, because wiring them together is its whole job. Dev PC
   Management and Sessions are here for their panes and nothing else — the
   shell names no tool type and no session type, so it takes each module's
   abstractions only for the feature key it gates on. Roadmap and Monitoring are
   here on the same terms, for the band and the dashboard: each brings one component
   and one feature key. *@
@using Backlog.Desktop.UI.Shell
@using Backlog.Desktop.UI.AppUpdate
@using Backlog.Desktop.UI.Inbox
@using Backlog.Desktop.UI.BacklogManagement
@using Backlog.Desktop.UI.Knowledge
@using Backlog.Modules.DevPc.UI
@using Backlog.Modules.Sessions.UI
@using Backlog.Modules.Roadmap.UI
@using Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.UI
@using Backlog.Modules.Dashboard.Abstractions
@* The feature port and the published surfaces the feature catalog gathers its
   keys from. Constants only: the shell reads no DTO and calls no port on any of
   them. *@
@using Backlog.SharedKernel
@using Backlog.Modules.Backlog.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.Knowledge.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.DevPc.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.Roadmap.Abstractions
@using Backlog.Modules.Sessions.Abstractions
